-//! Periodic re-synchronisation of a stored claim against finalized on-chain state.
-//!
-//! The event-driven path is reorg-safe on reads (the indexer ignores anything within
-//! 20 minutes of the head) but not on writes: `send_or_replace` returns on the first
-//! confirmation and the dispatcher then drops the task. A `Challenge` task only ever
-//! exists because `validate_claim` created one, and `validate_claim` removes itself as
-//! soon as it has done so - so if the challenge transaction is later reorged out, the
-//! `Challenged` event is never (re-)observed, `SendSnapshot` is never scheduled, and
-//! nothing re-examines the claim. The fraudulent claim then verifies unopposed.
-//!
-//! This task closes that hole. It re-reads the outbox at the **finalized** L1 block and
-//! compares it against the claim we have on file:
-//!
-//! - claim still unchallenged and our verdict says invalid -> schedule `Challenge`
-//! - our challenge is in the finalized chain but was never indexed -> repair the claim
-//!   record and schedule `SendSnapshot`, exactly as the `Challenged` handler would
-//!
-//! It never decides anything from mutable state: the claim state comes from the
-//! `finalized` tag, and the verdict from [`finalized_state_root`], which is the same
-//! finality-gated read `validate_claim` uses.
